From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buildroot STM32F429 demo <noreply@example.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: stm32f429: add flat include compatibility

Buildroot 2024.02 copies custom ARM device trees to arch/arm/boot/dts.
Linux 6.6 keeps the STM32F429 SoC and pinctrl includes in the st vendor
subdirectory, so custom device trees written for the Linux 6.1 layout can
no longer find them.

Add forwarding includes at the old paths. This keeps external device trees
compatible without duplicating the board description or making it depend on
the selected kernel version.

Signed-off-by: Buildroot STM32F429 demo <noreply@example.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429-pinctrl.dtsi | 2 ++
 arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429.dtsi         | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429-pinctrl.dtsi
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429.dtsi

--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429-pinctrl.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+/* Compatibility include for external device trees using the flat layout. */
+#include "st/stm32f429-pinctrl.dtsi"
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/stm32f429.dtsi
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+/* Compatibility include for external device trees using the flat layout. */
+#include "st/stm32f429.dtsi"
-- 
2.39.5

